clueweb09-en0007-85-36529.0 Dutchess County Tourism Search Events Calendar: Search Events by Location: All Amenia Annandale-on-Hudson Beacon Beekman Clinton Corners Dover Plains Fishkill Germantown Hopewell Junction Hyde Park LaGrange Lagrangeville Millbrook Millerton Pawling Pine Plains Pleasant Valley Poughkeepsie Poughquag Red Hook Rhinebeck Staatsburg Stanford Stormville Tivoli Wappingers Falls Wassaic Wingdale Press Room In the Spotlight StoryIdeas News Releases Photo Gallery Group Tours Advertise With Us Contact Us About Us Home HOW TO REACH US CONTACTS Dutchess County, New York is located halfway between New York City and Albany, New York, the state capitol, on the east bank of the Hudson River. Its one of only 14 designated National Heritage areas in the U.S. Its a ninety-minute drive, train or bus ride north from New York City or south from Albany, our state capitol. If anything piques your interest, I will be happy to provide further information. If you are going to be in our area and
clueweb09-en0007-85-36529.135 Dutchess County Tourism happy to provide further information. If you are going to be in our area and would like to visit attractions, I can assist you with itineraries. Dutchess County Tourism is a destination marketing organization located in the heart of the historic Hudson Valley. Heres how to reach us to find out more about Dutchess County. Press Inquiries: Nancy Lutz, Communications Manager 3 Neptune Rd. Suite Q-17 Poughkeepsie, NY 12601 845/463-5446 Phone 845/463-4064 Fax Nancy@DutchessTourism.com Publications: Dutchess County Travel Guide Farm Fresh Guide Scenic & Historic Drive Tours Bike Tours Happenings, four seasonal calendars of events PRESS ROOM CONTENTS >> In the Spotlight Story Ideas News Releases Photo Gallery About DCT | Advertise with Us | Contact Us | Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Home (C) 2006 Dutchess County Tourism. All rights reserved. Dutchess County Tourism, 3 Neptune Rd. Suite Q-17, Poughkeepsie NY 12601 Tel: 845/463-4000 or 800/445-3131 The
