clueweb09-en0005-00-32597.135  Traffic Safety Board Veterans Affairs Water and Wastewater Authority Youth Bureau [County Executive] Home . Search . County Government . Municipalities . Business . Schools . Tourism . Community . Elected Officials Click on an FAQ Category below to view questions and answers Text Size: [Normal Text Size] [Large Text Size] County Government >> About Dutchess County Printable version [FAQs image] - Frequently Asked Questions - About Dutchess County What is the climate of Dutchess County? What is the area of Dutchess County in square miles? What is the population of Dutchess County? Where can I find information about the cost of living in Dutchess County? Where can I find statistics on salaries in Dutchess County? What is the unemployment rate in Dutchess County? What Dutchess County jobs are currently open? Where are the county buildings located? What are the major tourist attractions in Dutchess County? Who are the elected
clueweb09-en0005-00-32597.270  buildings located? What are the major tourist attractions in Dutchess County? Who are the elected officials serving Dutchess County residents? About Dutchess County Q. What is the climate of Dutchess County? Dutchess Countys climate is moderate compared to other locations in the northeastern United States. Average temperatures range from a low of 18° F in January to high of 84° F in July. Go to top of page Q. What is the area of Dutchess County in square miles? The area of Dutchess County is 801.6 square miles. Click on the following link to view Land Area by municipality. Go to top of page Q. What is the population of Dutchess County? Based on the U.S. Census Bureau's last official census of 2000, the population of Dutchess County is 280,150. For 2005, the population of Dutchess County is projected to be 291,153 (Estimates by Poughkeepsie-Dutchess County Transportation Council, with base
clueweb09-en0005-00-32597.405  Dutchess County is projected to be 291,153 (Estimates by Poughkeepsie-Dutchess County Transportation Council, with base county data from NYMTC forecasting program, 2003). The Dutchess County Department of Planning and Development provides Census data on their webpages. Click on the following link to view a list of population information and other Census data. Go to top of page Q. Where can I find information about the cost of living in Dutchess County? For the most current information on the cost of living in Dutchess County, contact Dutchess County Economic Development Corporation at 3 Neptune Road, Poughkeepsie, N.Y. 12601, dcedc@dcedc.com, Phone: (845) 463-5410, Fax: (845) 463-5401. The US Department of Labor's Consumer Price Index program produces monthly data on changes in the prices paid by urban consumers for a representative basket of goods and services. Go to top of page Q. Where can I find statistics on salaries in Dutchess County? The
