clueweb09-en0005-00-32596.135  Elected Officials Text Size: [Normal Text Size] [Large Text Size] County Government >> Dutchess County Winter Heating Resource Guide (Print Version) [Dutchess County Government Cares]Dutchess County Winter Heating Resource Guide This resource guide is designed to help residents become smart winter energy consumers by offering tips and information about how families can lower their home heating bills through smart conservation and energy efficiency. You can also utilize these resources to determine your eligibility for a number of programs that may provide you with some assistance paying your winter energy bills. Conservation and Energy Saving Tips Dutchess County Department of Consumer Affairs has compiled a great list of hot tips for cold weather. Weatherization Referral and Packaging Program (WRAP) for Dutchess County residents 60 or older This program is designed to help senior citizens with energy related problems or needs. Home Energy Assistance Program (HEAP) HEAP is a federally funded program
clueweb09-en0005-00-32596.270  related problems or needs. Home Energy Assistance Program (HEAP) HEAP is a federally funded program intended to assist low-income households in meeting their energy expenses. Other Resources: For assistance completing HEAP applications, please contact: Community Action Agency Beacon area - (845) 831-2620 Poughkeepsie area - (845) 452-5104 Eastern Dutchess - (845) 877-9272 Northern Dutchess - (845) 876-1611 For last resort home heating fuel bill assistance, please contact: Dutchess Outreach Poughkeepsie - (845) 454-3792 -or- The Salvation Army (part of Central Hudson Gas & Electric Corporation Good Neighbor Fund ) Poughkeepsie - (845) 471-1210 Beacon - (845) 831-1253 Go to top of page - Home - | - Legal Statements - | - How to Use this Site - | - Contact Us - Last Updated: 9/18/2008
clueweb09-en0001-76-07256.0 Untitled Document Groups—Your Destination is Dutchess! Destination Dutchess Accommodations Restaurants Historical/Museums The Arts Gardens Culinary & Agricultural Outdoor Adventures [spacer] [spacer] Sacred Spaces [spacer] Itineraries Support Seasonal Historic Themed tours Students Senior Friendly FIT Tour Support Receptive Operators Escort Notes Motorcoach Services [spacer] [spacer] Request Assistance [spacer] [none] [none] [no image] [no image] [no image] [no image] Press Room Advertise With Us Contact DCT About DCT DutchessTourism.com Home Itineraries—Historic With its abundance of historic landmarks, Dutchess County is the perfect place for groups to experience the heritage of America. The area’s “Great Estates” are now museums, and historic homesteads tell the story of the American Revolution. Whether your group wants to visit a home owned by a millionaire, or the home of an ordinary citizen, we can help plan a tour that spans up to three centuries of history. About DCT | Advertise with Us | Contact Us | Privacy Policy |
