clueweb09-en0005-00-32668.0  ÿ Tourism:Culture and Arts [County Executive] Home . Search . County Government . Municipalities . Business . Schools . Tourism . Community . Elected Officials Text Size: [Normal Text Size] [Large Text Size] Tourism/Recreation >> Culture & Performing Arts Culture and Arts To Nourish the Soul... Our County has much to offer in the area of Culture and the Arts. Take time to visit a wide range of museums, art galleries, and cultural centers. In addition, our colleges and libraries sponsor exhibitions, lectures, performances, workshops and classes for all ages. One of the Countys attractions is the historic Bardavon 1869 Opera House which is Dutchess County's premier center for the performing arts and the home of the Hudson Valley Philharmonic. [Culture and Arts image] The arts community welcomes everyone to participate in cultural activities, on stage or behind the scenes. The Dutchess County Arts Council, an arts service organization, provides
clueweb09-en0005-00-32668.135  stage or behind the scenes. The Dutchess County Arts Council, an arts service organization, provides a calendar of events, workshops, and ARTSLINE, a 24-hour events hotline (845) 473-4ART. For other Arts Council information, call (845) 454-3222. - Home - | - Legal Statements - | - How to Use this Site - | - Contact Us - Last Updated: 3/11/2004
clueweb09-en0007-85-36543.0 Dutchess County Tourism - Wineries - Wine Trail Search Events Calendar: Search Events by Location: All Amenia Annandale-on-Hudson Beacon Beekman Clinton Corners Dover Plains Fishkill Germantown Hopewell Junction Hyde Park LaGrange Lagrangeville Millbrook Millerton Pawling Pine Plains Pleasant Valley Poughkeepsie Poughquag Red Hook Rhinebeck Staatsburg Stanford Stormville Tivoli Wappingers Falls Wassaic Wingdale [Wineries] Arts Campgrounds Children's Corner Drive-In Movies Farms & Markets Farmers Markets Fish & Game Gardens Golf Courses Hiking Historical / Museums Horseback Riding Hudson River Fun Multiple Use Areas Nightly Entertainment Parks Personal Growth [spacer] [spacer] Recreation [spacer] Shooting Clubs Shopping Spas Top Ten Lists Wineries Group Tours Press Room Advertise With Us Contact Us About Us Home [Dutchess County Wines]Discover each unique vineyard along the scenic Dutchess Wine Trail. Tours and tastings of award-winning wines await your palette. Alison Wines & Vineyards Description: Alison Wines produces award winning red and white wines, and dessert style wines from local strawberries and black currants. Hours: Seasonal
clueweb09-en0007-85-36543.135 Dutchess County Tourism - Wineries - Wine Trail and white wines, and dessert style wines from local strawberries and black currants. Hours: Seasonal hours. Location: 231 Pitcher Ln., Red Hook. Contact: 845/758-6335. URL: AlisonWines.com [Dutchess Wine Trail] Cascade Mountain Winery & Restaurant Description: A farm winery with tours and tastings, award winning wines and a critically acclaimed restaurant. Hours: Restaurant and winery hours are seasonal. Call for current schedule. Location: 835 Cascade Mountain Rd., Amenia. Contact: 845/373-9021 URL: CascadeMt.com Clinton Vineyards & Winery Description: Picturesque farm winery and vineyard, acclaimed Estate Bottled white wines, champagnes, cassis, and dessert wines. Tours and tastings year round. Hours: Thurs.-Mon., noon-5:30pm or by appt. for groups. Location: 450 Schultzville Rd., Clinton Corners. Contact: 845/266-5372 URL: ClintonVineyards.com Dutchess Wine Trail c/o Clinton Vineyards Description: Scenic country trail with stops along the way for tours and tastings at Alison Wines & Vineyards in Red Hook, Clinton Vineyards in Clinton Corners, and Millbrook Vineyards &
clueweb09-en0007-85-36543.270 Dutchess County Tourism - Wineries - Wine Trail Wines & Vineyards in Red Hook, Clinton Vineyards in Clinton Corners, and Millbrook Vineyards & Winery in Millbrook. Free trail guide. Location: 450 Schultzville Rd., Clinton Corners Contact: 845/266-5372 URL: DutchessWineTrail.com Millbrook Vineyards & Winery Description: Farm winery and vineyard with views of the Hudson Valley. Nationally recognized wines, Chardonnay, Tocai Frivlano, Pinot Noir, Cabernet Franc. Tours and tastings daily. Hours: Sept.-May noon-5pm, June-Aug, 11am-6pm. Location: 26 Wing Rd., Millbrook. Contact: 800-662-WINE URL: MillbrookWine.com Notes: Handicapped accessible Oak Summit Vineyard Description: Classic, estate bottled Pinot Noir in the traditional Burgundian manner. Location: 372 Oak Summit Rd., Millbrook. Contact: 845/677-9522 URL: www.oaksummitvineyard.com Notes: Tours by appointment only. Available for functions. Santo Stefano Winemaking Club Description: Patrons participate in winemaking sessions from crush to bottle. Wines are made without added sulfites, and are chemical-free. Personalized labels produced. Private tastings, catering available. Location: 44 St. Nicholas Road, Wappingers Falls. Contact: 845/297-2580 URL: SantoStefanoWinemaking.com
