clueweb09-en0007-85-36510.135 Dutchess County Tourism - Hiking About Us Home [Hiking in Dutchess County]Hiking and biking are great ways to promote health and enjoy the areas natural beauty, from the Catskill Mountains and Hudson River to the foothills of the Berkshires. Appalachian Trail Description: 30 miles of the Trail pass through southeastern Dutchess. 4,000 acres of protected parkland with hiking, backpacking, snowshoeing, cross-country skiing and five overnight use areas. Location: Look for trail crossing signs with triangle at: Rt. 52, 4 mi. east of the Taconic Parkway, parking on north side of road; Rt. 55, west of Pawling near Rt. 292 intersection, parking 1/4 mile west of trail crossing; Rt. 22, north of Pawling, between Rt. 68 & DOT parking area, north of Rt. 68 and Hurds Corners Rd. Brochure available. Contact: 201/512-9348 URL: NYNJTC.org Codes: F, D Harlem Valley Rail Trail Description: 22 miles (15 open) of scenic paved walking, rollerblading, biking and cross-country skiing trails,
clueweb09-en0007-85-36510.270 Dutchess County Tourism - Hiking Description: 22 miles (15 open) of scenic paved walking, rollerblading, biking and cross-country skiing trails, linking towns, villages and state parks on the rail bed from Wassaic Metro-North Station to Copake Falls. No horses or motorized vehicles allowed. Location: Access points; Railroad Plaza, Millerton, across from gazebo. In Amenia, Mechanic St., parking lot 2/10 of a mile on left. Also access at Wassaic Metro North Station and at Taconic State Park in Copake Falls. Contact: 518/789-9591 URL: HVRT.org Codes: D, F, G, H Historic Hyde Park Trail Description: Over 10 miles of trails link several parks and historic sites. Maps and information at trail heads, park visitor centers, and on-line. Bicycles not permitted. Location: Access points;  Home of Franklin D. Roosevelt National Historic Site  Vanderbilt Mansion NHS  Val-Kill NHS  Hackett Hill Town Park  Pinewoods Town Park  Riverfront Town Park Contact: 845/229-9115 or -8086 URL:
clueweb09-en0007-85-36510.405 Dutchess County Tourism - Hiking Town Park  Pinewoods Town Park  Riverfront Town Park Contact: 845/229-9115 or -8086 URL: www.hydeparkny.us/recreation/HealthyTrails.shtml Codes: F, G Hudson Valley Adventure Tours Description: Guided hiking tours offer views of the Hudson River and mountain ranges. Challenging and fun for singles, couples & families. Half-day $45, full-day $60. Includes round-trip train ticket out of Grand Central Station, NYC. Location: 27 Fieldstone Blvd., Wappingers Falls. Contact: 845/298-6234 or 888/445-3796 URL: HudsonValleyAdventureTours.com DEC Hudson River Research Reserve Description: 1,700 acre reserve, a wildlife management area and field laboratory for research and education about the Hudson River Estuary. Canoe the marsh, bicycle, observe wildlife or hike on one of six trails. Location: 256 Norrie Point Way, Staatsburg URL: DEC.State.NY.US Contact: 845/889-4745 The Nature Conservancy Description: Multi-acre reserves with miles of hiking trails, mountains, fields, woods and ponds. Preserve guide available. Location:  Nellie Hill Preserve, Rt. 22, Dover Plains.  Pawling Nature Reserve,
clueweb09-en0011-60-31197.0 Dutchess County, NY Search billions of records on Ancestry.com Welcome to [NYGenWeb logo - Dutchess] Designed by Jane Ann Smith Dutchess County [NY State Map] a proud part of the US GenWeb Dutchess County Search Engine Search this site or the web powered by FreeFind INPUT TYPE="TEXT" NAME="query" SIZE="20"> Site search Web search Announcements: Please note: I do not live in New York, and do not have any better access to Dutchess County records than you do. Check the links on this page for what records are available in the county and state, what others have donated to this Project and what records the Lookup Volunteers have. I have also listed mailing addresses and in many cases email addresses for Dutchess County -- Historical Societies, Genealogical Societies, Town Historians and where to write for vital records. You might also want to join the NYDUTCHE-L mailing list, as some of the listmembers own Dutchess
clueweb09-en0011-60-31197.135 Dutchess County, NY also want to join the NYDUTCHE-L mailing list, as some of the listmembers own Dutchess County publications and/or live in the area and can possibly help you in your search. They are a very helpful bunch. You can also post your query on the USGenNet Query Board. Subscribers to this list are also a very helpful bunch. Dutchess County USGenWeband ALHN/AHGP Message Boards: Queries/Surnames Wills/Deeds Obituaries Table of Contents About Dutchess County About the NY GenWeb Project About the US GenWeb Project Census Lookup Lists Crown Patent Map Dutchess County Bible Records Dutchess County Cemeteries. Dutchess County Deeds [Added August 16, 2007] Dutchess County Map Dutchess County Maps--- Old USGS Maps of Dutchess County Dutchess County Patent Map--- Courtesy of DCHS and Little Nine Partners HS. Dutchess County Photos Dutchess County Postcards Dutchess County---Old Poughkeepsie in Photos and Engravings Dutchess County Queries Unknown NY County Queries Dutchess County Resources Dutchess
clueweb09-en0011-60-31197.270 Dutchess County, NY in Photos and Engravings Dutchess County Queries Unknown NY County Queries Dutchess County Resources Dutchess County Soldiers and Sailors Dutchess County Surnames Dutchess County Town Histories, Biographies, and Memoirs Dutchess County Wills Lookup Volunteers New York Soldiers and Sailors New York State Resources Genealogy-Related Links Freedom of Information Act Can Help Where to Write for Vital Records About the US GenWeb Project The US GenWeb is a well organized effort to organize the genealogy materials on the Internet. This project is supported by hundreds of volunteers all across the county. Basically, the system is organized by states, and counties with each county having a coordinator responsible for maintaining a site of resources which are available for that county. You'll also find files of genealogy records, also organized by state and county. Back to Table of Contents About the New York GenWeb Project A message was sent out over the GEN-NYS-L
clueweb09-en0011-60-31197.405 Dutchess County, NY Contents About the New York GenWeb Project A message was sent out over the GEN-NYS-L list in June 1996 asking if anyone would be interested in starting a New York State GenWeb page similiar to a highly successful project underway in Kentucky. Many people expressed an interest in this idea. About the same time, Jeff Murphy, coordinator of the KY GenWeb, decided to go national with the idea, and out of that grew the US GenWeb project, and the NY GenWeb project. At the same time, volunteers were found who were willing to coordinate the collection of databases and generally oversee the contents of the web page. Contact the volunteer shown on the county page if you have a desire to add your data to the database. Back to Table of Contents About Dutchess County, New York Dutchess County was formed in 1683, one of the original counties of New
